cts.\\\\n| Action | Type| \\\\n|  --- | ---  |\\\\n| Trigger a function when a change is detected on a SQL table | [SQL trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-trigger) |\\\\n| Read data from a database | [Input binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-input) |\\\\n| Save data to a database | [Output binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-output) |\\\\n\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql#samples\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-python)\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-python)\\\\n## Samples\\\\nIn addition to the samples for C#, Java, JavaScript, PowerShell, and Python available in the [Azure SQL bindings GitHub repository](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-sql-extension/tree/main/samples), more are available in Azure Samples:\\\\n1. [ToDo API sample with Azure SQL bindings (C#)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/azure-samples/azure-sql-binding-func-dotnet-todo/todo-backend-dotnet-azure-sql-bindings-azure-functions/)\\\\n2. [Use SQL bindings in Azure Stream Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/stream-analytics/sql-database-upsert#option-1-update-by-key-with-the-azure-function-sql-binding)\\\\n# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-java)\\\\nThis set of articles explains how to work with [Azure SQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/index) bindings in Azure Functions. Azure Functions supports input bindings, output bindings, and a function trigger for the Azure SQL and SQL Server products.\\\\n| Action | Type| \\\\n|  --- | ---  |\\\\n| Trigger a function when a change is detected on a SQL table | [SQL trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-trigger) |\\\\n| Read data from a database | [Input binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-input) |\\\\n| Save data to a database | [Output binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-output) |\\\\n\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql#samples\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-powershell)\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-powershell)\\\\n## Samples\\\\nIn addition to the samples for C#, Java, JavaScript, PowerShell, and Python available in the [Azure SQL bindings GitHub repository](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-sql-extension/tree/main/samples), more are available in Azure Samples:\\\\n1. [ToDo API sample with Azure SQL bindings (C#)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/azure-samples/azure-sql-binding-func-dotnet-todo/todo-backend-dotnet-azure-sql-bindings-azure-functions/)\\\\n2. [Use SQL bindings in Azure Stream Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/stream-analytics/sql-database-upsert#option-1-update-by-key-with-the-azure-function-sql-binding)\\\\n# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-python)\\\\nThis set of articles explains how to work with [Azure SQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/index) bindings in Azure Functions. Azure Functions supports input bindings, output bindings, and a function trigger for the Azure SQL and SQL Server products.\\\\n| Action | Type| \\\\n|  --- | ---  |\\\\n| Trigger a function when a change is detected on a SQL table | [SQL trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-trigger) |\\\\n| Read data from a database | [Input binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-input) |\\\\n| Save data to a database | [Output binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-output) |\\\\n\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql#samples\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"What is Azure Functions?\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# What is Azure Functions?\\\\nAzure Functions is a serverless solution that allows you to build robust apps while using less code, and with less infrastructure and lower costs. Instead of worrying about deploying and maintaining servers, you can use the cloud infrastructure to provide all the up-to-date resources needed to keep your applications running.\\\\nYou focus on the code that matters most to you, in the most productive language for you, and Azure Functions handles the rest. For a list of supported languages, see [Supported languages in Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/supported-languages).\\\\n## Scenarios\\\\nFunctions provides a comprehensive set of event-driven [triggers and bindings](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-triggers-bindings) that connect your functions to other services without having to write extra code.\\\\nThe following list includes common integrated scenarios that use Functions.\\\\n| If you want to... | then...| \\\\n|  --- | ---  |\\\\n| [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads) | Run code when a file is uploaded or changed in blob storage. |\\\\n| [Process data in real time](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing) | Capture and transform data from event and IoT source streams on the way to storage. |\\\\n| [Run AI inference](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai) | Pull text from a queue and present it to various AI services for analysis and classification. |\\\\n| [Run scheduled task](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks) | Execute data clean-up code on predefined timed intervals. |\\\\n| [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api) | Implement a set of REST endpoints for your web applications using HTTP triggers. |\\\\n| [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow) | Create an event-driven workflow from a series of functions using Durable Functions. |\\\\n| [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes) | Run custom logic when a document is created or updated in a database. |\\\\n| [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems) | Process message queues using Azure Queue Storage, Service Bus, or Event Hubs. |\\\\n\\\\nThese scenarios allow you to build event-driven systems using modern architectural patterns. For more information, see [Azure Functions scenarios](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios).\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Azure Functions libraries for .NET\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Azure Functions libraries for .NET\\\\n## Overview\\\\n[Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview) is a solution for easily running small pieces of code, or *functions*, in Azure. Azure Functions supports a [serverless](https://azure.microsoft.com/solutions/serverless/) execution model.\\\\n## Durable Functions extension\\\\n*Durable Functions* is an extension of [Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview) that lets you write stateful functions in a serverless compute environment. The extension lets you define stateful workflows by writing [*orchestrator functions*](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/durable/durable-functions-orchestrations) and stateful entities by writing [*entity functions*](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/durable/durable-functions-entities) using the Azure Functions programming model. Behind the scenes, the extension manages state, checkpoints, and restarts for you, allowing you to focus on your business logic.\\\\nInstall the extension [NuGet package](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Microsoft.Azure.WebJobs.Extensions.DurableTask) directly from the Visual Studio [Package Manager console](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/nuget/tools/package-manager-console) or with the [.NET Core CLI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/tools/dotnet-add-package).\\\\nThe Azure API reference documentation supports [version 2.x of the Durable Functions extension](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/overview/azure/functions/runtime).\\\\n### Visual Studio package manager\\\\n\\\\u0060\\\\u0060\\\\u0060powershell\\\\nInstall-Package Microsoft.Azure.WebJobs.Extensions.DurableTask\\\\n\\\\u0060\\\\u0060\\\\u0060\\\\n### .NET Core CLI\\\\n\\\\u0060\\\\u0060\\\\u0060dotnetcli\\\\ndotnet add package Microsoft.Azure.WebJobs.Extensions.DurableTask\\\\n\\\\u0060\\\\u0060\\\\u0060\\\\n### Getting started\\\\n## Samples\\\\nView the [complete list](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/browse/?products=azure-functions\\\\u0026languages=csharp) of Azure Functions samples.\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/api/overview/azure/functions?view=azure-dotnet#overview\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-csharp)\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-csharp)\\\\nAzure Functions lets you implement your system\\\\u0027s logic as event-driven, readily available blocks of code. These code blocks are called functions. This article helps you find the most useful Azure Functions content quickly. For more general information about Azure Functions, see the [Introduction to Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview).\\\\nChoose your preferred development language at the top of the article.\\\\n## Create your first function\\\\nComplete a quickstart article to create and deploy your first functions in less than five minutes.\\\\nYou can create your first function by using one of the following tools:\\\\n1. [Azure Developer CLI (azd)](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/create-first-function-azure-developer-cli)\\\\n2. [Command line](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli)\\\\n3. [Visual Studio Code](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-vs-code)\\\\n4. [Visual Studio](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-create-your-first-function-visual-studio)\\\\n## Review end-to-end samples\\\\nThese sites let you browse existing functions reference projects and samples in your desired language:\\\\n1. [Awesome azd template library](https://azure.github.io/awesome-azd/?tags=functions\\\\u0026tags=dotnetCsharp)\\\\n2. [Azure Functions samples in GitHub](https://github.com/search?q=topic%3Aazure-functions\\\\u002Borg%3AAzure-Samples\\\\u002Bfork%3Atrue\\\\u002Blanguage%3AC%23\\\\u0026type=repositories\\\\u0026l=C%23)\\\\n3. [Azure samples browser](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/browse/?expanded=azure\\\\u0026languages=csharp\\\\u0026products=azure-functions)\\\\n## Scenarios\\\\nHere are some common scenarios to help you get started:\\\\n1. [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads)\\\\n2. [Real-time stream and event processing](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing)\\\\n3. [Machine learning and AI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai)\\\\n4. [Run scheduled tasks](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks)\\\\n5. [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api)\\\\n6. [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow)\\\\n7. [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes)\\\\n8. [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems)\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-get-started\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-javascript)\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-javascript)\\\\nAzure Functions lets you implement your system\\\\u0027s logic as event-driven, readily available blocks of code. These code blocks are called functions. This article helps you find the most useful Azure Functions content quickly. For more general information about Azure Functions, see the [Introduction to Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview).\\\\nChoose your preferred development language at the top of the article.\\\\n## Create your first function\\\\nComplete a quickstart article to create and deploy your first functions in less than five minutes.\\\\nYou can create your first function by using one of the following tools:\\\\n1. [Azure Developer CLI (azd)](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/create-first-function-azure-developer-cli)\\\\n2. [Command line](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli)\\\\n3. [Visual Studio Code](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-vs-code)\\\\n## Review end-to-end samples\\\\nThese sites let you browse existing functions reference projects and samples in your desired language:\\\\n1. [Awesome azd template library](https://azure.github.io/awesome-azd/?tags=functions\\\\u0026tags=javascript)\\\\n2. [Azure Functions samples in GitHub](https://github.com/search?q=topic%3Aazure-functions\\\\u002Borg%3AAzure-Samples\\\\u002Bfork%3Atrue\\\\u002Blanguage%3AJavaScript\\\\u0026type=repositories)\\\\n3. [Azure samples browser](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/browse/?expanded=azure\\\\u0026languages=javascript\\\\u0026products=azure-functions)\\\\n## Scenarios\\\\nHere are some common scenarios to help you get started:\\\\n1. [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads)\\\\n2. [Real-time stream and event processing](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing)\\\\n3. [Machine learning and AI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai)\\\\n4. [Run scheduled tasks](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks)\\\\n5. [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api)\\\\n6. [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow)\\\\n7. [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes)\\\\n8. [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems)\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-get-started\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Azure Functions diagnostics overview\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Azure Functions diagnostics overview\\\\nWhen you\\\\u2019re running a function app, you want to be prepared for any issues that may arise, from 4xx errors to trigger failures. Azure Functions diagnostics is an intelligent and interactive experience to help you troubleshoot your function app with no configuration or extra cost. When you do run into issues with your function app, Azure Functions diagnostics points out what\\\\u2019s wrong. It guides you to the right information to more easily and quickly troubleshoot and resolve the issue. This article shows you the basics of how to use Azure Functions diagnostics to more quickly diagnose and solve common function app issues.\\\\n## Start Azure Functions diagnostics\\\\nTo start Azure Functions diagnostics:\\\\n1. Navigate to your function app in the [Azure portal](https://portal.azure.com).\\\\n2. Select **Diagnose and solve problems** to open Azure Functions diagnostics.\\\\n3. Choose a category that best describes the issue of your function app by using the keywords in the homepage tile. You can also type a keyword that best describes your issue in the search bar. For example, you could type \\\\u0060execution\\\\u0060 to see a list of diagnostic reports related to your function app execution and open them directly from the homepage.\\\\n ![Search for Azure Functions diagnostics.](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/media/functions-diagnostics/functions-app-search-azure-functions-diagnostics.png)\\\\n## Use the Interactive interface\\\\nOnce you select a homepage category that best aligns with your function app\\\\u0027s problem, Azure Functions diagnostics\\\\u0027 interactive interface, named Genie, can guide you through diagnosing and solving problem of your app. You can use the tile shortcuts provided by Genie to view the full diagnostic report of the problem category that you\\\\u0027re interested in. The tile shortcuts provide you a direct way of accessing your diagnostic metrics.\\\\n![Genie is Azure Functions diagnostics\\\\u0027 interface.](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/media/functions-diagnostics/genie.png)\\\\nAfter selecting a tile, you can see a list of topics related to the issue described in the tile. These topics provide snippets of notable information from the full report. Select any of these topics to investigate the issues further. Also, you can select **View Full Report** to explore all the topics on a single page.\\\\n![Preview of diagnostic report](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/media/functions-diagnostics/preview-of-diagnostic-report.png)\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-diagnostics\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-go)\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-go)\\\\nAzure Functions lets you implement your system\\\\u0027s logic as event-driven, readily available blocks of code. These code blocks are called functions. This article helps you find the most useful Azure Functions content quickly. For more general information about Azure Functions, see the [Introduction to Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview).\\\\nChoose your preferred development language at the top of the article.\\\\n## Create your first function\\\\nComplete a quickstart article to create and deploy your first functions in less than five minutes.\\\\nYou can create your first function by using one of the following tools:\\\\n1. [Azure Developer CLI (azd)](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/create-first-function-azure-developer-cli)\\\\n2. [Command line](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli)\\\\n3. [Visual Studio Code](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-vs-code)\\\\nGet started with Go on Azure Functions:\\\\n1. [Command line quickstart](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli?pivots=programming-language-go)\\\\n## Review end-to-end samples\\\\n1. [Azure Functions Go worker samples](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-golang-worker/tree/main/samples)\\\\n## Scenarios\\\\nHere are some common scenarios to help you get started:\\\\n1. [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads)\\\\n2. [Real-time stream and event processing](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing)\\\\n3. [Machine learning and AI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai)\\\\n4. [Run scheduled tasks](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks)\\\\n5. [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api)\\\\n6. [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow)\\\\n7. [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes)\\\\n8. [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems)\\\\n## Explore an interactive tutorial\\\\nComplete one of the following interactive training modules to learn more about Functions:\\\\n1. [Well-Architected Framework - Performance efficiency](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/azure-well-architected-performance-efficiency/)\\\\n2. [Azure Functions triggers and bindings](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-triggers-bindings)\\\\nTo learn even more, see the [full listing of interactive tutorials](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/browse/?expanded=azure\\\\u0026products=azure-functions).\\\",\\\"contentUrl\\\":\\\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-get-started\\\"}]}\"}],\"structuredContent\":{\"results\":[{\"title\":\"Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-csharp)\",\"content\":\"# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-csharp)\\n## Samples\\nIn addition to the samples for C#, Java, JavaScript, PowerShell, and Python available in the [Azure SQL bindings GitHub repository](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-sql-extension/tree/main/samples), more are available in Azure Samples:\\n1. [ToDo API sample with Azure SQL bindings (C#)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/azure-samples/azure-sql-binding-func-dotnet-todo/todo-backend-dotnet-azure-sql-bindings-azure-functions/)\\n2. [Use SQL bindings in Azure Stream Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/stream-analytics/sql-database-upsert#option-1-update-by-key-with-the-azure-function-sql-binding)\\n# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-javascript)\\nThis set of articles explains how to work with [Azure SQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/index) bindings in Azure Functions. Azure Functions supports input bindings, output bindings, and a function trigger for the Azure SQL and SQL Server products.\\n| Action | Type| \\n|  --- | ---  |\\n| Trigger a function when a change is detected on a SQL table | [SQL trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-trigger) |\\n| Read data from a database | [Input binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-input) |\\n| Save data to a database | [Output binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-output) |\\n\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql#samples\"},{\"title\":\"Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-javascript)\",\"content\":\"# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-javascript)\\n## Samples\\nIn addition to the samples for C#, Java, JavaScript, PowerShell, and Python available in the [Azure SQL bindings GitHub repository](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-sql-extension/tree/main/samples), more are available in Azure Samples:\\n1. [ToDo API sample with Azure SQL bindings (C#)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/azure-samples/azure-sql-binding-func-dotnet-todo/todo-backend-dotnet-azure-sql-bindings-azure-functions/)\\n2. [Use SQL bindings in Azure Stream Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/stream-analytics/sql-database-upsert#option-1-update-by-key-with-the-azure-function-sql-binding)\\n# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-powershell)\\nThis set of articles explains how to work with [Azure SQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/index) bindings in Azure Functions. Azure Functions supports input bindings, output bindings, and a function trigger for the Azure SQL and SQL Server products.\\n| Action | Type| \\n|  --- | ---  |\\n| Trigger a function when a change is detected on a SQL table | [SQL trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-trigger) |\\n| Read data from a database | [Input binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-input) |\\n| Save data to a database | [Output binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-output) |\\n\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql#samples\"},{\"title\":\"Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-python)\",\"content\":\"# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-python)\\n## Samples\\nIn addition to the samples for C#, Java, JavaScript, PowerShell, and Python available in the [Azure SQL bindings GitHub repository](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-sql-extension/tree/main/samples), more are available in Azure Samples:\\n1. [ToDo API sample with Azure SQL bindings (C#)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/azure-samples/azure-sql-binding-func-dotnet-todo/todo-backend-dotnet-azure-sql-bindings-azure-functions/)\\n2. [Use SQL bindings in Azure Stream Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/stream-analytics/sql-database-upsert#option-1-update-by-key-with-the-azure-function-sql-binding)\\n# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-java)\\nThis set of articles explains how to work with [Azure SQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/index) bindings in Azure Functions. Azure Functions supports input bindings, output bindings, and a function trigger for the Azure SQL and SQL Server products.\\n| Action | Type| \\n|  --- | ---  |\\n| Trigger a function when a change is detected on a SQL table | [SQL trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-trigger) |\\n| Read data from a database | [Input binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-input) |\\n| Save data to a database | [Output binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-output) |\\n\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql#samples\"},{\"title\":\"Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-powershell)\",\"content\":\"# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-powershell)\\n## Samples\\nIn addition to the samples for C#, Java, JavaScript, PowerShell, and Python available in the [Azure SQL bindings GitHub repository](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-sql-extension/tree/main/samples), more are available in Azure Samples:\\n1. [ToDo API sample with Azure SQL bindings (C#)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/azure-samples/azure-sql-binding-func-dotnet-todo/todo-backend-dotnet-azure-sql-bindings-azure-functions/)\\n2. [Use SQL bindings in Azure Stream Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/stream-analytics/sql-database-upsert#option-1-update-by-key-with-the-azure-function-sql-binding)\\n# Azure SQL bindings for Azure Functions overview (programming-language-python)\\nThis set of articles explains how to work with [Azure SQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/index) bindings in Azure Functions. Azure Functions supports input bindings, output bindings, and a function trigger for the Azure SQL and SQL Server products.\\n| Action | Type| \\n|  --- | ---  |\\n| Trigger a function when a change is detected on a SQL table | [SQL trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-trigger) |\\n| Read data from a database | [Input binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-input) |\\n| Save data to a database | [Output binding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql-output) |\\n\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-azure-sql#samples\"},{\"title\":\"What is Azure Functions?\",\"content\":\"# What is Azure Functions?\\nAzure Functions is a serverless solution that allows you to build robust apps while using less code, and with less infrastructure and lower costs. Instead of worrying about deploying and maintaining servers, you can use the cloud infrastructure to provide all the up-to-date resources needed to keep your applications running.\\nYou focus on the code that matters most to you, in the most productive language for you, and Azure Functions handles the rest. For a list of supported languages, see [Supported languages in Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/supported-languages).\\n## Scenarios\\nFunctions provides a comprehensive set of event-driven [triggers and bindings](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-triggers-bindings) that connect your functions to other services without having to write extra code.\\nThe following list includes common integrated scenarios that use Functions.\\n| If you want to... | then...| \\n|  --- | ---  |\\n| [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads) | Run code when a file is uploaded or changed in blob storage. |\\n| [Process data in real time](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing) | Capture and transform data from event and IoT source streams on the way to storage. |\\n| [Run AI inference](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai) | Pull text from a queue and present it to various AI services for analysis and classification. |\\n| [Run scheduled task](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks) | Execute data clean-up code on predefined timed intervals. |\\n| [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api) | Implement a set of REST endpoints for your web applications using HTTP triggers. |\\n| [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow) | Create an event-driven workflow from a series of functions using Durable Functions. |\\n| [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes) | Run custom logic when a document is created or updated in a database. |\\n| [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems) | Process message queues using Azure Queue Storage, Service Bus, or Event Hubs. |\\n\\nThese scenarios allow you to build event-driven systems using modern architectural patterns. For more information, see [Azure Functions scenarios](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios).\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview\"},{\"title\":\"Azure Functions libraries for .NET\",\"content\":\"# Azure Functions libraries for .NET\\n## Overview\\n[Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview) is a solution for easily running small pieces of code, or *functions*, in Azure. Azure Functions supports a [serverless](https://azure.microsoft.com/solutions/serverless/) execution model.\\n## Durable Functions extension\\n*Durable Functions* is an extension of [Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview) that lets you write stateful functions in a serverless compute environment. The extension lets you define stateful workflows by writing [*orchestrator functions*](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/durable/durable-functions-orchestrations) and stateful entities by writing [*entity functions*](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/durable/durable-functions-entities) using the Azure Functions programming model. Behind the scenes, the extension manages state, checkpoints, and restarts for you, allowing you to focus on your business logic.\\nInstall the extension [NuGet package](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Microsoft.Azure.WebJobs.Extensions.DurableTask) directly from the Visual Studio [Package Manager console](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/nuget/tools/package-manager-console) or with the [.NET Core CLI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/tools/dotnet-add-package).\\nThe Azure API reference documentation supports [version 2.x of the Durable Functions extension](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/overview/azure/functions/runtime).\\n### Visual Studio package manager\\n```powershell\\nInstall-Package Microsoft.Azure.WebJobs.Extensions.DurableTask\\n```\\n### .NET Core CLI\\n```dotnetcli\\ndotnet add package Microsoft.Azure.WebJobs.Extensions.DurableTask\\n```\\n### Getting started\\n## Samples\\nView the [complete list](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/browse/?products=azure-functions&languages=csharp) of Azure Functions samples.\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/api/overview/azure/functions?view=azure-dotnet#overview\"},{\"title\":\"Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-csharp)\",\"content\":\"# Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-csharp)\\nAzure Functions lets you implement your system's logic as event-driven, readily available blocks of code. These code blocks are called functions. This article helps you find the most useful Azure Functions content quickly. For more general information about Azure Functions, see the [Introduction to Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview).\\nChoose your preferred development language at the top of the article.\\n## Create your first function\\nComplete a quickstart article to create and deploy your first functions in less than five minutes.\\nYou can create your first function by using one of the following tools:\\n1. [Azure Developer CLI (azd)](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/create-first-function-azure-developer-cli)\\n2. [Command line](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli)\\n3. [Visual Studio Code](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-vs-code)\\n4. [Visual Studio](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-create-your-first-function-visual-studio)\\n## Review end-to-end samples\\nThese sites let you browse existing functions reference projects and samples in your desired language:\\n1. [Awesome azd template library](https://azure.github.io/awesome-azd/?tags=functions&tags=dotnetCsharp)\\n2. [Azure Functions samples in GitHub](https://github.com/search?q=topic%3Aazure-functions+org%3AAzure-Samples+fork%3Atrue+language%3AC%23&type=repositories&l=C%23)\\n3. [Azure samples browser](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/browse/?expanded=azure&languages=csharp&products=azure-functions)\\n## Scenarios\\nHere are some common scenarios to help you get started:\\n1. [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads)\\n2. [Real-time stream and event processing](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing)\\n3. [Machine learning and AI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai)\\n4. [Run scheduled tasks](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks)\\n5. [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api)\\n6. [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow)\\n7. [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes)\\n8. [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems)\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-get-started\"},{\"title\":\"Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-javascript)\",\"content\":\"# Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-javascript)\\nAzure Functions lets you implement your system's logic as event-driven, readily available blocks of code. These code blocks are called functions. This article helps you find the most useful Azure Functions content quickly. For more general information about Azure Functions, see the [Introduction to Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview).\\nChoose your preferred development language at the top of the article.\\n## Create your first function\\nComplete a quickstart article to create and deploy your first functions in less than five minutes.\\nYou can create your first function by using one of the following tools:\\n1. [Azure Developer CLI (azd)](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/create-first-function-azure-developer-cli)\\n2. [Command line](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli)\\n3. [Visual Studio Code](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-vs-code)\\n## Review end-to-end samples\\nThese sites let you browse existing functions reference projects and samples in your desired language:\\n1. [Awesome azd template library](https://azure.github.io/awesome-azd/?tags=functions&tags=javascript)\\n2. [Azure Functions samples in GitHub](https://github.com/search?q=topic%3Aazure-functions+org%3AAzure-Samples+fork%3Atrue+language%3AJavaScript&type=repositories)\\n3. [Azure samples browser](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/samples/browse/?expanded=azure&languages=javascript&products=azure-functions)\\n## Scenarios\\nHere are some common scenarios to help you get started:\\n1. [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads)\\n2. [Real-time stream and event processing](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing)\\n3. [Machine learning and AI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai)\\n4. [Run scheduled tasks](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks)\\n5. [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api)\\n6. [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow)\\n7. [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes)\\n8. [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems)\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-get-started\"},{\"title\":\"Azure Functions diagnostics overview\",\"content\":\"# Azure Functions diagnostics overview\\nWhen you’re running a function app, you want to be prepared for any issues that may arise, from 4xx errors to trigger failures. Azure Functions diagnostics is an intelligent and interactive experience to help you troubleshoot your function app with no configuration or extra cost. When you do run into issues with your function app, Azure Functions diagnostics points out what’s wrong. It guides you to the right information to more easily and quickly troubleshoot and resolve the issue. This article shows you the basics of how to use Azure Functions diagnostics to more quickly diagnose and solve common function app issues.\\n## Start Azure Functions diagnostics\\nTo start Azure Functions diagnostics:\\n1. Navigate to your function app in the [Azure portal](https://portal.azure.com).\\n2. Select **Diagnose and solve problems** to open Azure Functions diagnostics.\\n3. Choose a category that best describes the issue of your function app by using the keywords in the homepage tile. You can also type a keyword that best describes your issue in the search bar. For example, you could type `execution` to see a list of diagnostic reports related to your function app execution and open them directly from the homepage.\\n ![Search for Azure Functions diagnostics.](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/media/functions-diagnostics/functions-app-search-azure-functions-diagnostics.png)\\n## Use the Interactive interface\\nOnce you select a homepage category that best aligns with your function app's problem, Azure Functions diagnostics' interactive interface, named Genie, can guide you through diagnosing and solving problem of your app. You can use the tile shortcuts provided by Genie to view the full diagnostic report of the problem category that you're interested in. The tile shortcuts provide you a direct way of accessing your diagnostic metrics.\\n![Genie is Azure Functions diagnostics' interface.](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/media/functions-diagnostics/genie.png)\\nAfter selecting a tile, you can see a list of topics related to the issue described in the tile. These topics provide snippets of notable information from the full report. Select any of these topics to investigate the issues further. Also, you can select **View Full Report** to explore all the topics on a single page.\\n![Preview of diagnostic report](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/media/functions-diagnostics/preview-of-diagnostic-report.png)\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-diagnostics\"},{\"title\":\"Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-go)\",\"content\":\"# Get started with Azure Functions (programming-language-go)\\nAzure Functions lets you implement your system's logic as event-driven, readily available blocks of code. These code blocks are called functions. This article helps you find the most useful Azure Functions content quickly. For more general information about Azure Functions, see the [Introduction to Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-overview).\\nChoose your preferred development language at the top of the article.\\n## Create your first function\\nComplete a quickstart article to create and deploy your first functions in less than five minutes.\\nYou can create your first function by using one of the following tools:\\n1. [Azure Developer CLI (azd)](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/create-first-function-azure-developer-cli)\\n2. [Command line](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli)\\n3. [Visual Studio Code](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-vs-code)\\nGet started with Go on Azure Functions:\\n1. [Command line quickstart](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/how-to-create-function-azure-cli?pivots=programming-language-go)\\n## Review end-to-end samples\\n1. [Azure Functions Go worker samples](https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-golang-worker/tree/main/samples)\\n## Scenarios\\nHere are some common scenarios to help you get started:\\n1. [Process file uploads](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#process-file-uploads)\\n2. [Real-time stream and event processing](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#real-time-stream-and-event-processing)\\n3. [Machine learning and AI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#machine-learning-and-ai)\\n4. [Run scheduled tasks](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#run-scheduled-tasks)\\n5. [Build a scalable web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-scalable-web-api)\\n6. [Build a serverless workflow](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#build-a-serverless-workflow)\\n7. [Respond to database changes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#respond-to-database-changes)\\n8. [Create reliable message systems](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-scenarios#create-reliable-message-systems)\\n## Explore an interactive tutorial\\nComplete one of the following interactive training modules to learn more about Functions:\\n1. [Well-Architected Framework - Performance efficiency](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/azure-well-architected-performance-efficiency/)\\n2. [Azure Functions triggers and bindings](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-triggers-bindings)\\nTo learn even more, see the [full listing of interactive tutorials](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/browse/?expanded=azure&products=azure-functions).\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-functions/functions-get-started\"}]},\"isError\":false}"}},"event_type":"step.delta"}

